<Subpage
  title="Privacy: nothing you type leaves your computer"
  description="Nothing you type leaves your computer. unflub counts how it's used, never what you write, and you can switch that off in one click."
  crumb="Privacy"
>
  <h1>Nothing you type leaves your computer.</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    unflub counts how it's used, never what you write, and you can switch that off in one click. This page lists everything it
    sends.
  </p>

  <h2>What you type</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Corrections are worked out on your computer. Your text is never sent anywhere.</li>
    <li>
      unflub holds the word you are typing, and the one before it for context, in memory. It never writes what you type to disk.
    </li>
    <li>
      Password fields are always skipped. Terminals and password managers are skipped by default, and you can add any other app.
    </li>
    <li>There's no account and no advertising ID. We don't sell or share data, and unflub shows no ads.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>On by default, off in one click</h2>
  <p>
    These help us find bugs and see which settings people use. One switch on the General page in Settings turns off both.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Usage stats.</strong> Counts, such as corrections per day, how often a fix gets undone, which settings are on and
      how long a check takes. Never a word you typed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Crash reports.</strong> If unflub crashes, it sends where in the code it failed. Any text is scrubbed out first.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The daily update check</h2>
  <p>Once a day, unflub asks whether a newer version is out. The request carries this and nothing else:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the unflub version, such as {SITE.version}</li>
    <li>your Windows version and processor type, x64 or ARM</li>
    <li>
      a random install ID, made when you install unflub. It isn't based on your name, your account, your hardware or anything
      you type. It lets us count how many computers run unflub without counting one twice.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>Turn off Automatic updates on the About page in Settings and unflub stops checking.</p>

  <h2>Off unless you turn it on: Help improve corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If you switch this on, unflub shares anonymous typo and fix pairs, like <em>teh</em> to <em>the</em>. It only sends pairs
    where both words are common dictionary words, never names or numbers. We keep a pair only once at least 5 different installs
    have sent it, so a slip that only you make is never stored.
  </p>

  <h2>Your Stats page stays home</h2>
  <p>
    The Stats page in the app shows your corrections this week, the words you get wrong most and how many keystrokes unflub
    saved you. It is worked out and kept on your computer, and none of it is sent.
  </p>

  <h2>Your settings</h2>
  <p>
    Your settings, your words and your shortcuts are saved in a file on your computer. Uninstalling unflub removes the app and its
    login entry, and the uninstaller asks whether to delete that file too.
  </p>

  <h2>Check for yourself</h2>
  <p>
    unflub is open source, so you do not have to take our word for any of this. <a href={SITE.repo}>Read the code on GitHub</a>,
    or <a href={SITE.issues}>open an issue</a> if you have a question.
  </p>

  <p class="small updated">Last updated November 2026. unflub is an <a href={SITE.org.url}>RMGN</a> product.</p>
</Subpage>

